# Log Line Constructor

Here's a JavaScript function that builds a formatted log line:

```javascript
/**
 * Constructs a log line from a level, message, and timestamp.
 *
 * @param {string} level - e.g. "INFO", "WARN", "ERROR"
 * @param {string} message - the log message
 * @param {Date} [timestamp=new Date()] - optional; defaults to now
 * @returns {string} formatted log line
 */
function formatLogLine(level, message, timestamp = new Date()) {
  if (!level || typeof level !== 'string') {
    throw new TypeError('level must be a non-empty string');
  }

  const pad = (n, width = 2) => String(n).padStart(width, '0');

  const date = `${timestamp.getFullYear()}-${pad(timestamp.getMonth() + 1)}-${pad(timestamp.getDate())}`;
  const time = `${pad(timestamp.getHours())}:${pad(timestamp.getMinutes())}:${pad(timestamp.getSeconds())}.${pad(timestamp.getMilliseconds(), 3)}`;

  return `[${date} ${time}] [${level.toUpperCase().padEnd(5)}] ${message}`;
}
```

## Example usage

```javascript
console.log(formatLogLine('info', 'Server started on port 3000'));
// [2025-01-15 14:32:07.042] [INFO ] Server started on port 3000

console.log(formatLogLine('error', 'Database connection failed', new Date('2025-01-15T10:00:00Z')));
// [2025-01-15 10:00:00.000] [ERROR] Database connection failed
```

