## Design notes

- **Timestamp normalization** — accepts a `Date`, epoch milliseconds, or any string `new Date()` can parse; invalid values throw a `TypeError` rather than silently producing `Invalid Date`.
- **Level casing** — normalized to uppercase by default, since `info`/`INFO`/`Info` are the same level in practice.
- **Custom timestamp format** — pass `formatTimestamp` to use local time, epoch seconds, or your own layout without touching the core function.
- **Multi-line messages** — if a message contains `\n`, the continuation lines won't be prefixed. If that matters, either escape newlines (`message.replace(/\n/g, '\\n')`) or split the message and format each line separately.

